    "answer": {
      "short": "Perfect: $6$.\n\nAbundant: $12,18,20$.\n\nDeficient: $1,2,3,4,5,7,8,9,10,11,13,14,15,16,17,19$.",
      "worked": "Compare each number with the sum of its positive proper divisors. For $1$, there are no positive proper divisors, so the sum is $0$.\n\n$1$: $0<1$ — deficient.\n\n$2$: $1<2$ — deficient.\n\n$3$: $1<3$ — deficient.\n\n$4$: $1+2=3<4$ — deficient.\n\n$5$: $1<5$ — deficient.\n\n$6$: $1+2+3=6$ — perfect.\n\n$7$: $1<7$ — deficient.\n\n$8$: $1+2+4=7<8$ — deficient.\n\n$9$: $1+3=4<9$ — deficient.\n\n$10$: $1+2+5=8<10$ — deficient.\n\n$11$: $1<11$ — deficient.\n\n$12$: $1+2+3+4+6=16>12$ — abundant.\n\n$13$: $1<13$ — deficient.\n\n$14$: $1+2+7=10<14$ — deficient.\n\n$15$: $1+3+5=9<15$ — deficient.\n\n$16$: $1+2+4+8=15<16$ — deficient.\n\n$17$: $1<17$ — deficient.\n\n$18$: $1+2+3+6+9=21>18$ — abundant.\n\n$19$: $1<19$ — deficient.\n\n$20$: $1+2+4+5+10=22>20$ — abundant.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
